I'd avoid dividing £100 across three paid platforms. You could end up with too little evidence from any of them.

For the TikTok creative, make the opening slide identify the buyer immediately: UK electricians who own their own business—still doing quotes at 9 pm? Then demonstrate an actual workflow rather than explain AI in the abstract.

Your `/content` project already has much of the rendering infrastructure needed. The additional work is exporting native slideshows, creating several hooks per offer and recording which creative produces booked calls.

The first meaningful metric is cost per qualified conversation with a trades-business owner, followed by cost per paying customer. I'd record organic enquiries alongside paid results so you can identify where the sales are actually coming from.

For now, your planned direct calls remain an important comparison: they involve no advertising spend, let you hear objections immediately and can help refine the message before putting money behind it.
